/-!
# Generated Gram data for the standard rank-15 hosts

One block per lattice: the three norm-one-free cores `E8`, `D12+`, `(E7+E7)+`
and the five rank-15 hosts
`Z^15`, `E8 + Z^7`, `D12+ + Z^3`, `(E7+E7)+ + Z`, `A15+`.

Each block carries

* `<h>CoordsData` -- a basis in *scaled* integer coordinates, one row per basis
  vector.  A lattice vector `x` is stored as `scale * x`, so the pairing is
  `<x,y> = (scale x) . (scale y) / scale ^ 2`.
* `<h>GramData` -- the Gram matrix of that basis, and `<h>GramInvData` its
  integer inverse;
* `<h>LdltFactorData`, `<h>LdltWeightData`, `<h>LdltScale` -- an exact
  integer-scaled LDLT certificate in the shape of
  `SRG266.checkIntegerScaledGram`.

All of it is data.  Every identity is re-checked by the kernel in
`SRG266/Lattice/Hosts/*.lean`; nothing about the generator is trusted.
-/

